## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Category                  | Technology                                   |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Runtime                   | Node.js                                      |
| Framework                 | Express.js                                   |
| Database                  | MongoDB & Mongoose                           |
| Caching                   | Redis                                        |
| Real-time                 | Socket.IO                                    |
| Authentication & Security | JWT, bcrypt, rate-limiting                   |
| Email Services            | Nodemailer (OTPs & verification)             |
| File Uploads              | Multer                                       |
| File Storage              | Cloudinary                                   |
| Background Jobs           | BullMQ, PDFKit (written-note PDF generation) |
| Containerization          | Docker                                       |

---

## 📂 Folder Structure

```text
backend/
├── public/                 # Static files
├── src/
│   ├── controllers/        # Route logic and request handling
│   ├── db/                 # Database connection setup (MongoDB)
│   ├── middlewares/        # Custom middlewares (auth, rate limits, multer, etc.)
│   ├── models/             # Mongoose schemas and models
│   ├── queues/             # BullMQ queue definitions
│   ├── routes/             # Express route definitions
│   ├── utils/              # Helper functions, custom error/response classes
│   ├── workers/            # BullMQ background workers (written-note PDF generation)
│   ├── app.js              # Express app setup and middleware configuration
│   ├── constants.js        # Global constants (DB names, etc.)
│   └── index.js            # Main entry point, server & Socket.IO initialization
├── tests/                  # Backend integration test suite (node:test)
│   ├── routes/             # Per-resource route tests
│   └── test-utils.js       # Shared test helpers
├── .dockerignore           # Files to ignore in Docker builds
├── .env                    # Environment variables (do not commit this!)
├── .env.example            # Template for environment variables
├── .gitignore              # Files to ignore in Git
├── .prettierignore         # Files to ignore for Prettier
├── .prettierrc             # Prettier formatting rules
├── Dockerfile.backend      # Docker configuration for containerization
├── package-lock.json       # Exact dependency versions
└── package.json            # Project dependencies and scripts
```

